00BCE to 20AD or so when the companion comes out. I had a lot of material that I had to cut for wordcount, and I'm not sure exactly what events/dates made it in off hand. I'd give you my notes after the book comes out but only what's in the book counts as official, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:00:39-07:00","id":912090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=910590#post910590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love this timeline! You *should* (I hope) be able to piece together Uratha history around Italy and Scandinavia from roughly 1200BCE to 20AD or so when the companion comes out. I had a lot of material that I had to cut for wordcount, and I'm not sure exactly what events/dates made it in off hand. I'd give you my notes after the book comes out but only what's in the book counts as official, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Wolves of Rome I take it? Roman History was one of the focuses of my History major, so I'm REALLY looking forward to that chapter and the Cleopatran Mummy chapter. <br /> <br /> I've been super busy with work lately, and will be for the next two weeks as our year winds down, but I'm going to take this moment to pop in a brief outline for Bowery Dogs. Also, I'd like to say thank you for all of the support. I'm pretty jazzed that people like this, especially when freelancers say how cool it is to see their writing visually. Makes my day!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T05:44:32-07:00","id":912749,"title":"","content":"Does dark era's cover world war one ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:10:53-07:00","id":913020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=912749#post912749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does dark era's cover world war one ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish. Closest thing I can think of--someone correct me if I'm wrong--is a small bit I put into the Grimm Dark Era chapter. It's just a reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:24:24-07:00","id":913026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=913020#post913020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish. Closest thing I can think of--someone correct me if I'm wrong--is a small bit I put into the Grimm Dark Era chapter. It's just a reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ruins of Empire covers WWI, the collapse of the Ottoman Empire, and the waning of the English and French Empires at the same time, but the focus is on the Empires and not the War. Goodbye to All That in Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries for Vampire does cover WWI, and there is a brief shout out to that era in Night Stalkers under the same name. I'm actually working on two version of the timeline fore this period... one for the extended events and entities, and one for the blow by blow breakdown of the War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:07:24-07:00","id":913734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=912090#post912090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome! Wolves of Rome I take it? Roman History was one of the focuses of my History major, so I'm REALLY looking forward to that chapter and the Cleopatran Mummy chapter.<br /> <br /> [snip]... especially when freelancers say how cool it is to see their writing visually. Makes my day!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yep, Roman Uratha and Germanic Uratha are the most detailed - well, as detailed as we could get in the word count. So much good stuff for Uratha/WoD history in that thousand year period. And the chapter lightly touches other locations around Europe and the Mediterranean. #spoilers<br /> <br /> So fo timeline creating awesomeness like you're doing, I dunno exactly how useful the 'brief touches' will be, nor do I know how much made it in to the book after development. But I do know, as a fan of historical things, that it was a blast to write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:57:41-07:00","id":913768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=913734#post913734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yep, Roman Uratha and Germanic Uratha are the most detailed - well, as detailed as we could get in the word count. So much good stuff for Uratha/WoD history in that thousand year period. And the chapter lightly touches other locations around Europe and the Mediterranean. #spoilers<br /> <br /> So fo timeline creating awesomeness like you're doing, I dunno exactly how useful the 'brief touches' will be, nor do I know how much made it in to the book after development. But I do know, as a fan of historical things, that it was a blast to write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I can get broad strokes, my Roman History is good enough that I can fill in the facts myself to create something useful. So excited!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:25:02-07:00","id":920170,"title":"","content":"It has been a while, but I have good news! The first major patch for Aeon 2 showed up a week ago, and while I don't think it has directly addressed the bug that was screwing with my image files, between the update and debugging with the creator of the program via email, I seem to have resolved the glitch. That means I have not one, but three new timelines added today: <b>The Mighty Despair</b>, <b>Black Streets of Babylon</b>, and <b>To the Strongest</b>. <br /> <br /> First, a note on chronology. If you look at the dates for a lot of the ancient civilizations in the former two timelines on Wikipedia, you will find different dates than the ones that I use here. the exact date seen of ancient Mesopotamia is uncertain, although when the events happen relative to one another is well known. As a result, there are three broad groups of dates that scholars of Mesopotamian history used to try and establish a timeline: the short chronology, the middle chronology, and the long chronology. Each has different pros and cons, and while most scholars reject it now, Wikipedia tends to use the short chronology when giving its dates (although being Wikipedia it isn't always consistent). for my timeline, I have used a variation of the middle chronology, specifically the middle-low chronology. Now as a full disclaimer, while I do have a history degree, it is primarily in Roman, Islamic, and Scientific history, so I have never worked with Mesopotamian history academically, and I definitely do not have the astronomy background that is required to properly assess the data that was used to establish the middle-low chronology. It could be completely wrong. I happen to like it for building the chronological timeline, and for primary reading that I've done seems convincing to me. I strongly encourage you to read <a href=\"https://www.academia.edu/5453019/Astronomical_Fine-tuning_of_the_Chronology_of_the_Hammurabi_Age_2013_?auto=download\" target=\"_blank\">this paper </a>and make up your minds for yourselves. It's a good read and really opened my eyes to the types of techniques and information that are available to Mesopotamian historians and archaeologists. <br /> <br /> With all of that out of the way, let's look at the eras. The Mighty Despair and Black Streets of Babylon are both connected to timeline of the Rise of the Covenants by the presence of one character: En Isiratuu. With a Requiem of nearly 1,200 years, En Isiratuu casts a long shadow from the rise of Babylon under Hammurabi to its collapse in the Neo-Babylonian Empire. It is entirely possible that En Isiratuu was even Hammurabi himself, twisted by the embrace of the Kindred. <br /> <br /> En Isiratuu likely doesn't play a huge role in The Mighty Dispair, but as the Arisen move farther from Egypt in the Second Sothic Turn, It is entirely possible that they run afoul of the vampire king. you'll also notice that the reigns of David, Solomon, and Saul in the Mighty Despair are different colours from those of their contemporary rulers. This is because the archaeological evidence for those three kings points to their reigns being highly mythical. I've recorded the biblical reigns in the timeline but change the colour to indicate that they likely do not match with the historical reigns. I do feel their inclusion is appropriate, however, as they provide many storytelling opportunities, and King Solomon has been mentioned a number of times in Mage the Awakening. Personally, throw down between David and Solomon with En Isiratuu sounds like a pretty bad ass setting to me, and that's before you add the cosmic horror mummies to the mix!<br /> <br /> Black Streets of Babylon is a really interesting era. Since it encompasses the entirety of En Isiratuu's requiem, there are a lot of different stories worth telling, but something interesting happens in the middle of it. Remember the uncertain timeline I talked about at the start of the post? It disappears. The dates start to coalesce and become less uncertain. By the time you hit the years that are the focus of Black Streets of Babylon, of there is no uncertainty. We have transitioned from an era of myth and legend to a time of certain history. This gets driven home by the individuals who appear as En Isiratuu and Babylon finally fall: Astyages, Cyrus, Darius, and Xerxes. Mesopotamia no longer belongs to the Babylonians once En Isiratuu exits the stage. It is now, and still is, the domain of the Persians. <br /> <br /> This ties Black Streets very powerfully to To the Strongest. While the death of Alexander is the focus of the Era, the meeting of the Persian, Greek, Egyptian, and Indian Mages is in many ways catalysed by the actions of Darius and Xerxes in response to Athenes in the Ionian Wars. Darius reigns and Xerxes is born a measly 50 years after \u200bEn Isiratuu meets his final death. That's some powerful linkage. I should also note that To the Strongest is very incomplete at this point, I still have lots of Alexander's campaigns to expand on and add it, but for now, it should help to supply a broad image of what is happening at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T11:52:14-07:00","id":944977,"title":"","content":"I'm in between trips (just got back from Tanzania, just about to head to Iceland), so I'm back with one more timeline update. <br /> <br /> Today, I've added the <b>Lost Generation</b>, the Vampire era about the 30 Year War. Ancient Mysteries isn't too heavy on details, but I've been able to tease out some key facts, and will probably add to the timeline as I become more familiar with this period and can infer when more events occurred. This era is also interesting because it will be updated in the Dark Eras Companion by way of the backer created Promethean era. I was a little put out when it was first announced because we already had the 30 Year War in Vampire. That changed today, however, when I realized that one Rabbi Loew lived right before the war. We already knew that we'd be getting some details on the birth of the Frankensteins from A Year Without Summer. It seems we may also hear about the most famous of Tammuz as well. <br /> PS: Also, there is a rumour of Dark Eras 2 being confirmed at GenCon. Keep you fingers crossed!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T19:44:22-08:00","id":1028381,"title":"","content":"Time keeps on ticking... <br /> <br /> Today I have added one of my favourite eras, <b>Beneath the Skin</b>. I've covered some of the major events side of the timeline and region proper to give an idea of European encroachment into the region in case a storyteller wants to travel a bit further afield or wants to continue a chronicle after the era proper has ended. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_bl