/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T15:16:02-07:00","id":1456908,"title":"","content":"I noticed an error in the Brazilian Highlands timeline. The Vice-royalty of Peru didn't lasted there until 1842. In practice it was expelled in the early 1600's, replaced by conflicts between Brazilian &quot;Bandeirantes&quot; and mostly independent Jesuits. In the late 1600's and early to middle 1700's the Portuguese crown established formal colonies all over the place and in 1750 the treatise of Madri recognized it as Brazilian territory.<br /> <br /> Among other things this makes a difference because for the Spaniards and Jesuits enslaving natives was a crime, the Jesuits particularly worked with the natives, while the Bandeirantes enslaved and massacred them with overwhelming force and violence, which would make a lot of difference in a CoD game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The same applies for the Amazon Basin, but a little earlier due to a lack of economic interest in the region by Spain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-15-2021, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T03:09:38-07:00","id":1456941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=1456908#post1456908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed an error in the Brazilian Highlands timeline. The Vice-royalty of Peru didn't lasted there until 1842. In practice it was expelled in the early 1600's, replaced by conflicts between Brazilian &amp;quot;Bandeirantes&amp;quot; and mostly independent Jesuits. In the late 1600's and early to middle 1700's the Portuguese crown established formal colonies all over the place and in 1750 the treatise of Madri recognized it as Brazilian territory.<br /> <br /> Among other things this makes a difference because for the Spaniards and Jesuits enslaving natives was a crime, the Jesuits particularly worked with the natives, while the Bandeirantes enslaved and massacred them with overwhelming force and violence, which would make a lot of difference in a CoD game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The same applies for the Amazon Basin, but a little earlier due to a lack of economic interest in the region by Spain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, good catch, thank you! It probably won't get updated in this thread for a while, I'm waiting for the new version of the software I use to get out of beta (or at least far enough through it we can share our timelines) so that exporting is easier. But will make sure the date gets corrected when it finally happens.<br /> <br /> Also, I did eventually correct those broken links Baaldam pointed out, I just neglected to make a post about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T16:28:27-07:00","id":1456983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=1456941#post1456941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo, good catch, thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome!<br /> <br /> Advantages on having internet forums with people all over the world, I'm actually <i>from</i> the Brazilian Highlands, so when I saw the timeline it got my attention immediately and a quick search confirmed my suspicions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T19:06:42-07:00","id":1462601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/877339-the-eras-of-chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-and-others?p=1456983#post1456983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome!<br /> <br /> Advantages on having internet forums with people all over the world, I'm actually <i>from</i> the Brazilian Highlands, so when I saw the timeline it got my attention immediately and a quick search confirmed my suspicions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so digging back into this, the problem is a limitation of the software I'm using, I can't show VRofP being in the region in the early days without it also showing up in the later period. But what I CAN do is show the historical events representing the withdrawal of Peru from the region and the establishment of the Portuguese (including the Treaty of Madrid). It's not a perfect solution, but hopefully it will show some more clarity for the region and I'll keep noodling on if there is a way to breakup the Vice-Royalty's timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T07:47:37-07:00","id":1511449,"title":"","content":"It has been a spell, but I'm hoping to return for a long overdue update in the summer. In the meanwhile, I've started a little complementary project: a fully zoomable map of CofD locations that have been covered, including those in Dark Eras. I added the link to the first post a couple of days ago (to give it time for the spam filter to clear), but I'll post it below as well. Intent is not only to highlight which places have signature settings, but give a sense of geography for the locations within those settings. That sentance didn't make sense, but if you zoom in on Halifax, you'll see what I mean. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://u.osmfr.org/m/903366/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://u.osmfr.org/m/903366/\" target=\"_blank\"> Chronicles of Darkness </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://u.osmfr.o